  "review_findings_fixed": [
    "Retention conservatively preserves every historical job snapshot tuple and all replication sources, not merely newest backups or current jobs",
    "Preview digest includes exact manifest bytes, filesystem identity and replication pin set; candidate identity rechecked before deletion",
    "Restricted operator message verbs checked before replication; refusal test proves zero uploads and no attempted marker, avoiding a false pass from a later transport failure",
    "Replication verifies private source/spool ownership and uses weighted host admission before archive or network work"
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    "Combined preflight demonstrated new replication pins invalidate older retention previews; harness now tests refusal then refreshes preview",
    "Python runtime lacks tar extractall filter argument; harness explicitly validates every member is a regular relative path without parent traversal before extraction"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only explicit operator plane-backup retention is implemented; externally retained scratch archives and Git archive refs are never pruned. No automatic retention schedule or remote service retention policy is installed.",
    "Historical snapshot coverage and monotonic replication-source pins may retain more than keep. No unpin API exists.",
    "Interrupted partial directory deletion fails closed and needs operator investigation. Same-user malicious filesystem races are outside the ownership contract.",
    "A crash after durable attempt but before upload remains uncertain; absence of remote object never authorizes automatic reupload. SIGKILL may leave a private archive spool requiring operator inspection/removal.",
    "Remote protocol is configurable HTTPS or literal-loopback HTTP; no vendor or credential manager was selected. Native and dogfood network effects use disposable localhost fixtures.",
    "Receipt plus full archive checksum establishes equality with locally restore-tested bytes, not future remote availability or remote storage durability. Dogfood additionally restores the downloaded archive and runs Dolt fsck.",
    "Formal proofs cover production predicates and bounded lifecycle models, not complete HTTP, filesystem, Dolt, Git or provider internals."
  ],
